content.text:
Icons look good. Copy to repo icons/.

Now write manifest and sw. Also update server. Let's plan exact index edits.

index head:
`<link rel="preconnect" ...><link href="fonts..." rel="stylesheet"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">`

Add after viewport:
`<meta name="theme-color" content="#202020"><meta name="description" content="DiceForge Studio — live dice strategy desk for Crypto.Games."><meta name="application-name" content="DiceForge"><meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes"><meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="DiceForge"><meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent"><meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes"><link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.webmanifest"><link rel="icon" href="/icons/favicon-32.png" sizes="32x32" type="image/png"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icons/apple-touch-icon.png">`

Header: `<div class="top-status"><i></i><span id="topStatus">OFFLINE</span><button id="logout">↪</button></div>`
Add install button: `<button id="installBtn" class="install-btn" type="button" aria-label="Install DiceForge app" title="Install app" hidden>⤓</button>` before logout. Could use icon `⤓` or `↓`. Add CSS for `.install-btn` maybe same as top-status button; existing selector `.top-status button` covers it. We can add a gold color when shown: `.top-status .install-btn{color:var(--gold);border-color:#8a742e}`. Add at end of styles.css (new lines) plus maybe standalone safe area.

Also add install card to Info tab? Nice discoverability. Perhaps add a card in Account under "Bot behavior" or Info: `<div class="card install-card" id="installCard" hidden>... <button id="installCardBtn">INSTALL APP</button>...`. Simpler: only header button plus browser menu. But "Install web app" maybe expected a visible button. Header icon is discoverable but subtle. Add an install banner/card on Info or Account? Let's add a compact install card in Info with a button and platform hints. It can share handler. But hidden if already installed. Add to Info section before info-card:

`<div class="card install-card" id="installCard" hidden><div class="settings-intro"><span class="settings-icon">⤓</span><div><b>Install DiceForge</b><small>Jalankan sebagai aplikasi mandiri, tanpa address bar, dan tetap terbuka saat offline.</small></div></div><button class="primary" id="installCardBtn" type="button">INSTALL APP →</button><p class="install-hint" id="installHint">Gunakan menu browser “Install app” jika tombol tidak tersedia.</p></div>`

Need styles `.install-card` etc. Use existing classes mostly. Add `#installCard[hidden]{display:none}` (hidden default works unless display overrides; `.card` doesn't set display, hidden works).

App.js install logic appended at end (single line). Need be careful with existing code one line. We can append after `restoreSession();`:
```
let deferredInstallPrompt=null;const standalone=matchMedia('(display-mode: standalone)').matches||navigator.standalone===true;function canInstall(){...}
```
Need not re-declare `$` (already global). Define functions.

Implementation:

```
let installPrompt=null,installed=false;
const isStandalone=()=>matchMedia('(display-mode: standalone)').matches||navigator.standalone===true;
function showInstallUI(show){['installBtn','installCard'].forEach(id=>{const el=$(id);if(el)el.hidden=!show});}
function installHints(){ ... }
async function promptInstall(){ if(!installPrompt){ alert('...'); return; } installPrompt.prompt(); const {outcome}=await installPrompt.userChoice; if(outcome==='accepted'){ installPrompt=null; showInstallUI(false);} }
window.addEventListener('beforeinstallprompt',e=>{e.preventDefault();installPrompt=e;if(!isStandalone())showInstallUI(true)});
window.addEventListener('appinstalled',()=>{installPrompt=null;installed=true;showInstallUI(false);text('topStatus','APP INSTALLED')? no maybe not});
```
If iOS show install card with hint and button that alerts instructions. Actually if no installPrompt but iOS Safari and not standalone, show UI so they can read instructions. In promptInstall, if no prompt, show hint message / alert. Use `text('installHint', ...)` and maybe `alert`. Alert acceptable but ugly. Create message inline and unhide card. Since card visible, button click can update hint and focus.

Better:
```
function installUnavailableMessage(){
 const ua=navigator.userAgent;
 if(/iphone|ipad|ipod/i.test(ua)) return 'Di Safari: ketuk tombol Share lalu “Add to Home Screen”.';
 if(/firefox/i.test(ua)) return 'Firefox desktop belum mendukung instalasi PWA. Gunakan Chrome atau Edge.';
 return 'Gunakan menu browser (⋮) lalu pilih “Install app” / “Add to Home screen”.';
}
async function promptInstall(){
 if(!installPrompt){text('installHint',installUnavailableMessage());$('installCard')?.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return;}
 ...
}
```
Show UI:
- `beforeinstallprompt` -> show header button + card.
- if iOS and not standalone -> show card (and header button maybe) on load, with hint. Determine after DOM ready script already at end.
- if standalone -> hide.
- else initially maybe keep hidden until event; but on browsers that don't fire beforeinstallprompt (Safari) show card on iOS only. Good.
- `appinstalled` -> hide.

Register SW:
```
if('serviceWorker' in navigator){window.addEventListener('load',()=>{navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js').catch(()=>{})})}
```
Actually app.js executes at end of body; load event may have fired? Use direct register after checking `document.readyState === 'complete'` or just call immediately. Register immediately is fine:
```
if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js').catch(console.warn)
```
Avoid console noise maybe.

Update top status? no.

Also `#installBtn` inside top-status before logout, so existing logout handler still works. The header has `justify-content:space-between`; adding button okay.

Styles: `.install-btn{color:var(--gold)!important;border-color:#7d6a2b!important;background:#2a2618!important}` maybe. Existing `.top-status button` has margin-left:10px; install button and logout both get margin-left 10. Fine.

For install card, use existing settings-intro and primary. Add `.install-card .primary{margin-top:4px}` maybe. Add `.install-hint{...}`. Add `@media(display-mode: standalone){body{padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top)}}`? Could add safe-area padding to `.top`. Not necessary.

Service worker:

```
const CACHE='diceforge-v1';
const CORE=['/','/index.html','/styles.css','/app.js','/manifest.webmanifest','/icons/icon-192.png',...];
self.addEventListener('install',e=>{e.waitUntil(caches.open(CACHE).then(c=>c.addAll(CORE)).then(()=>self.skipWaiting()))});
self.addEventListener('activate',e=>{e.waitUntil(caches.keys().then(keys=>Promise.all(keys.filter(k=>k!==CACHE).map(k=>caches.delete(k)))).then(()=>self.clients.claim()))});
self.addEventListener('fetch',e=>{
 const req=e.request;
 if(req.method!=='GET')return;
 const url=new URL(req.url);
 if(url.origin!==location.origin||url.pathname.startsWith('/api/'))return;
 if(req.mode==='navigate'){
   e.respondWith(fetch(req).then(res=>{ if(res.ok){const copy=res.clone();caches.open(CACHE).then(c=>c.put('/index.html',copy));} return res;}).catch(async()=>await caches.match(req)||await caches.match('/index.html')||new Response(offlineHtml,{headers:{'Content-Type':'text/html; charset=utf-8'}})));
   return;
 }
 e.respondWith(caches.match(req).then(cached=>{const network=fetch(req).then(res=>{if(res.ok){const copy=res.clone();caches.open(CACHE).then(c=>c.put(req,copy));}return res;}).catch(()=>cached);return cached||network;}));
});
```
`addAll` fails if any asset missing, which prevents install. Ensure all exist. The query version `/app.js?v=...` isn't precached exactly; core '/app.js' okay, runtime caches versioned. Fine.

Offline navigation: When offline, `caches.match(req)` may match `/` if URL `/`. `caches.match('/index.html')`. Good. If app opened at `/?source=pwa` offline, `caches.match(req)` ignores search? cache.match default ignoreSearch false, so no; then index fallback.

One concern: caching navigation response under `/index.html` while response URL is `/?source=pwa`; cache.put('/index.html', copy) works. Good.

No API caching.

Manifest icons. Include `purpose: "any"` and maskable.

Maybe add `handle_links`, `launch_handler` not needed. `display_override` maybe not supported but fine.

`theme_color` #202020. `background_color` #111111.

Server MIME update and perhaps add header `Service-Worker-Allowed` for `/sw.js`? Scope root by default since at root. Fine.

Let's create files.

