Now, potential issue with SW caching `/index.html` in networkFirst: it stores response under `/index.html` but the response is for navigation to `/?tab=info`; body same. Fine.

Potential issue: Service worker caches app shell including `/app.js` but index references `/app.js?v=...`; install precache of `/app.js` unused except offline fetch of `/app.js?v=...` will not match and then network fails -> offline page loads but app.js missing! Wait: offline navigation falls back to cached `/index.html`, which references `/app.js?v=20261031-pwa3`. The SW intercepts that request. `caches.match(request)` with URL including query won't match `/app.js` (ignoreSearch false). Then it tries network, fails, returns `cached` which is undefined -> response becomes undefined, causing a network error; app JS won't load offline. Our earlier offline test showed page loaded with logo and install card? That was after app.js had been cached at the versioned URL by stale-while-revalidate during online visits. On a fresh install where the user installs then goes offline before loading the versioned app.js? During install, CORE includes `/app.js` (unversioned), but page load fetches versioned, so it gets cached during the first online load. Since installing requires loading the page, the versioned app.js will have been cached. Still, safer to cache both `/app.js` and versioned? SW can't know version. Better: in `staleWhileRevalidate`, on network failure, fall back to cache match ignoring search or `/app.js` / `/styles.css` by pathname. Or precache the exact versioned URL. Simpler: change index to reference `/app.js` without query (server no-store anyway), eliminating version mismatch. But cache-busting query is used deliberately. We can set SW fallback:

```
async function staleWhileRevalidate(request){
 const cache=...
 let cached=await cache.match(request);
 if(!cached){
   const url=new URL(request.url);
   cached=await cache.match(url.pathname);
 }
 ...
}
```
This makes versioned app.js fall back to unversioned precached. Also styles no query. Good. And after successful network, cache.put(request) versioned. Fine.

Also for navigation, `cache.put('/index.html', response.clone())` stores under absolute? cache.put accepts relative string resolved against SW scope. Fine.

Another issue: `cache.addAll(CORE)` includes '/' and '/index.html' duplicates, fine. If any fails install fails. All exist.

Add fallback by pathname. Also cache navigation response under both `/index.html` and request? Already networkFirst returns response but doesn't cache request URL; only index. That's fine.

Let's modify SW `staleWhileRevalidate`. Also bump CACHE version to v2 so existing test caches update, though no real users. Use v2.

Also consider fonts: external Google Fonts not cached, offline falls back to sans-serif. Fine. Could cache fonts but not needed.

Another issue: Service worker `fetch` handles requests for extension etc. Fine.

Potential issue with `request.mode === 'navigate'` and POST? filtered GET.

Potential security: SW caches `/api/` excluded.

Let's update.

